Structural and end-to-end tests for the real IOCTL_AFD_CONNECT input layout.

  afd_connect_layout_test.sh   host test; extracts struct
                               afd_connect_info_params_64/_32 from
                               ../include/wine/afd.h and re-parses requests
                               built from them using only documented byte
                               offsets.  Device-free, no Wine needed.

  afd_connect_e2e.c            ntdll-only PE probe; run under a Wine build from
                               this tree, once as x86_64 and once as i386.
                               Case A: a good native-layout connect succeeds.
                               Case B: a truncated request is rejected with
                                       STATUS_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL.
                               Case C: a ReactOS-layout request -- the same
                                       layout on i386 (must still succeed),
                                       12 bytes short on x86_64 (must fail).

Always run Wine binaries with WINEDEBUG=-all WINEDLLOVERRIDES=winedbg.exe=d
and stdin from /dev/null, and with a private WINEPREFIX.
